jobs.description:
The Vice President of Global Accounting is responsible for defining and leading the company’s global accounting strategy, overseeing global financial accounting, financial reporting, accounting policies, consolidated financial statements, and cross-regional accounting operations. By establishing unified accounting standards, strengthening financial control systems, and optimizing global accounting processes, this role ensures that financial information across all countries and regions is accurate, timely, and compliant with applicable accounting standards and regulatory requirements—thereby providing reliable support for corporate financial decision-making, risk management, and global business development.

This position typically oversees the global accounting function and regional accounting teams, working in close collaboration with the CFO, Corporate Controller, and the tax and financial management teams.

Core Responsibilities

I. Global Accounting Strategy and Policy Management
- Develop the company’s global accounting strategy and long-term development plans;
- Establish unified global accounting policies, accounting standards, and financial management systems;
- Drive the standardization of accounting processes across all countries and regions;
- Ensure that global accounting policies comply with US GAAP, IFRS, and relevant local accounting standards;
- Adjust the global accounting management framework in alignment with the company’s business development.

II. Global Financial Reporting and Consolidated Financial Statements
- Oversee financial reporting across all global business units and regional entities;
- Supervise the monthly, quarterly, and annual financial closing processes;
- Manage and review global consolidated financial statements;
- Ensure the accuracy, completeness, and consistency of financial data;
- Coordinate the collection, reconciliation, and reporting of financial information across regions.

III. Accounting Operations and Ledger Management
- Supervise general ledger, accounts receivable, accounts payable, and fixed asset accounting;
- Optimize global accounting workflows and financial closing cycles;
- Establish mechanisms for the review of accounting vouchers, account reconciliation, and the resolution of discrepancies;
- Drive the implementation of global shared financial services and the standardization of accounting operations;
- Enhance the efficiency of accounting processes and the quality of financial operations.

IV. Internal Control and Financial Compliance
- Establish and refine a global accounting internal control framework;
- Oversee key control measures within financial accounting and reporting processes;
- Ensure global accounting operations comply with relevant financial regulations and supervisory requirements;
- Coordinate external audits, internal audits, and financial compliance reviews;
- Drive the remediation of audit findings and the mitigation of accounting-related risks.

V. Cross-Border Financial Coordination and Technical Management
- Coordinate accounting teams and finance leads across various countries and regions;
- Supervise foreign currency translation, cross-border transactions, and intercompany accounting;
- Promote the implementation of ERP systems, financial management platforms, and automated accounting tools;
- Optimize global financial data management and reporting systems;
- Collaborate with tax, treasury, and corporate finance departments.

VI. Team Building and Organizational Management
- Build and lead a global accounting management team;
- Manage senior personnel, including Regional Controllers, Global Accounting Directors, and Accounting Managers;
- Define performance objectives and talent development plans for the global accounting team;
- Facilitate the sharing of best practices across regional accounting teams;
- Establish unified professional standards and efficient collaboration mechanisms.

Qualifications

Education
- Bachelor’s degree or higher in Accounting, Financial Management, Finance, or a related field;
- MBA, Master’s degree in Accounting, or a Master’s degree in Financial Management is preferred;
- Professional certifications such as CPA, CA, or ACCA are preferred;
- Proficiency in US GAAP, IFRS, and international financial reporting standards.

Work Experience
- 20+ years of experience in accounting, financial reporting, or corporate financial management;
- 15+ years of experience in senior accounting management or leading global finance teams;
- Prior experience in senior executive roles—such as VP of Global Accounting, VP of Corporate Accounting, or Corporate Controller—is preferred;
- Experience with multinational corporations, multi-entity accounting, and the management of global consolidated financial statements;
- Experience in global financial process integration, ERP system implementation, and the transformation of accounting operations;
- Experience collaborating with CFOs, audit committees, and external audit firms is preferred.

Core Competencies
- Global Accounting Management;
- Financial Reporting & Consolidation;
- US GAAP & IFRS;
- General Ledger Management;
- International Accounting Operations;
- Internal Controls & Compliance;
- Multi-Entity Accounting;
- Foreign Currency Translation;
- ERP & Financial Systems;
- Financial Process Optimization;
- Audit Coordination;
- Global Team Leadership.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
- Accuracy rate of global financial reporting;
- Cycle time for monthly and annual financial close;
- On-time delivery rate of global consolidated financial statements;
- Accounting error rate;
- Timeliness rate of account reconciliations;
- Compliance rate for the implementation of global accounting policies;
- Completion rate for the remediation of audit findings;
- Financial process automation rate;
- Cost control rate for global accounting operations;
- Performance achievement rate of the global accounting team.

